      "side": 1,
      "message": "This early return will allow the host to trigger executing `pkvm_vcpu_pvmfw_entry_init()` or `pkvm_vcpu_ap_entry_init()` more than once (since `kvm_vcpu_has_run()` is still false)? Although it _seems_ that wouldn\u0027t be harmful, since currently both `pkvm_vcpu_pvmfw_entry_init()` or `pkvm_vcpu_ap_entry_init()` implementations are \"idempotent\". But still it seems cleaner, and potentially safer, to avoid allowing that?\n\nFurthermore, we don\u0027t really need the CR3/PDPTR setup here, we only need to load the EPT?\n\nSo maybe we\u0027d better just call `kvm_x86_call(load_mmu_pgd)()` instead of `pkvm_load_mmu_pgd()` here?",
      "revId": "f393bebdd3097b25b477075b23e06795659a2efc",
